        {
            "block_label": "figure_title",
            "block_content": "<div style=\"text-align: center;\">To characterize MIA-scFM sensitivity as a function of overfitting, we trained a small scFM (BERT-style encoder;  $ L = 4 $ layers,  $ d = 128 $ embedding,  $ h = 4 $ heads,  $ d_{\\mathrm{ff}} = 512 $;  $ 4.3 \\times 10^6 $ parameters; mask ratio  $ \\rho = 0.15 $) from scratch under three regimes on disjoint Genecorpus-30M subsets, with known held-in / held-out membership labels (Table 3).</div>\n",
